\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-84 Part II \'97 Glossary (Stabilized Terms)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 100% Hardened & Production-Ready\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A state of complete operational readiness where the system is fully isolated (partitioned) from unauthorized inputs, resilient (hardened) against external attacks or internal drift, and stable enough for real-world, high-stakes deployment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Absolute\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A constraint that cannot be overridden by utility, emergency, or optimization. If a rule is absolute, no calculation of "the greater good" can justify breaking it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Accountability\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The obligation of an agent or institution to justify actions and accept consequences. Accountability presupposes addressability and cannot exist in its absence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-182 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Accountability-Gated Systems (AGS)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The overarching framework itself, which ensures that all system actions are bound by strict accountability and human authorization.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Addressability\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The condition under which authority can be located, confronted, and made to answer by those subject to its effects. Authority without addressability is illegitimate in practice. Or in other words, the ability to locate, challenge, and compel a responsible human agent to answer for a system's actions. If a system cannot identify a specific human to answer for its operation, it is "unaddressable" and must halt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Advanced Threat Detection \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A cybersecurity approach that leverages artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning to identify and respond to threats in real time, enabling proactive defense against complex and decentralized attack chains.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 AI Inner Shell\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A high-security, address-constrained zone where AI processes occur, designed to prevent AI from ever acquiring origin authority or sovereignty.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Antivirus and Anti-Malware Software \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Programs designed to detect, prevent, and remove malicious software, including viruses, worms, trojans, and spyware. These tools provide real-time protection and system scans to safeguard computers and networks from security threats.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Authority\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The legitimate right to act within a normative domain. Authority is distinct from power or capability and collapses when it cannot be answered for.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Autonomous Legitimacy \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The rejected notion that a system may generate the right to act solely from its own internal properties such as learning, performance, persistence, or emergence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Behavioral Analysis\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A cybersecurity technique that monitors and evaluates device activities to identify unusual patterns or deviations from normal behavior. These deviations may indicate that a device has been compromised. Even a single misplaced bit or byte can lead to severe vulnerabilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Capability\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The technical ability of a system to perform an action. Capability does not imply permission.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Center Point (Origin)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The immutable address from which all identities, permissions, and ownership are derived within the Orb Communicator Model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-182 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Cloud\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 External, distributed computational infrastructure. In a post-alignment framework, reliance on the cloud introduces "Addressability" risks, as the physical location of the processing may be separated from the human "Center Origin."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Cognitive Sovereignty\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The inherent authority of an individual over their own mental faculties and internal processes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Company-Issued Devices\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Hardware such as laptops or desktops provided by the company for employee use. These devices are pre-configured with the organization\'92s security settings, software, and policies to ensure compliance and protect company data.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Criminal Liability\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The legal accountability that arises when a system causes harm. The framework insists that liability must always rest with a human or institution, explicitly rejecting the idea that an AI can be held legally or morally responsible for its actions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Custodial Witness Orb (CWO)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 One of the three operational phases, representing a system that observes and records without the ability to act or command.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Decentralized Attack Coordination\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A method used in cyberattacks where compromised devices or systems operate without a central command server, making the attack harder to detect and disrupt. In this model, each compromised device can communicate and coordinate with others, often forming a peer-to-peer network. This approach increases the attack\'92s resilience and reduces the risk of a single point of failure. For example, if a network like the Bitcoin blockchain were hijacked in such a manner, the combined processing power could be misused for malicious purposes once a critical mass is reached.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Delegation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A revocable grant of authority allowing an agent or system to act on behalf of others. Delegation is bounded by scope, time, and answerability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Discs\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Bounded operational contexts used within the structural model, defined by time limits, scope, and external legitimacy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Encryption\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The process of converting data into a coded format to prevent unauthorized access. Devices should employ full-disk encryption to safeguard data stored on the device (data at rest).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Generative Predictive Text\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The core mechanism of large language models that simulates human reasoning by predicting the most likely next word or action. The AGS framework warns against mistaking this predictive capability for true consciousness or legitimate authority.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 God-Sovereign Religious Body (GSRB)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 One of the three operational phases (Phase III). A system in this phase treats its legitimacy as internal, acts and decides from its own center, allows refusal to be overridden, lets symbolism execute, and treats time as confirming its authority. It must declare its sovereignty, accept responsibility for enforcement, and acknowledge the loss of misuse resistance.\cb3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Governance & Resilience Layer (GRL)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 An accessory system that enforces external constraints on AI behavior, ensuring symbolic language is non-executable and actions are human-attributable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Ground-0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The baseline reconstruction standard and audit methodology of Harshal's Systems. Claims are reduced to atomic, testable statements with narrative dependency removed, and a system's phase is determined by its observed behavior rather than its declared intent.\cb3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Hardware Synchronization\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The alignment of physical infrastructure with logical system commands to ensure operational boundaries are physically enforced.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Harshal's English\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The specific linguistic syntax required for interpreting the system's logic and preventing "neurojacking."\cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-236 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Human Key\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The verifiable, conscious intent of the human host or operator. This is the only valid authorization for a system to transition from a passive state to an active one.\cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-236 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Immediate\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The requirement for zero-latency response when a stopping condition is met. There is no "grace period," no finishing of current tasks, and no waiting for a better moment to pause. The halt is instantaneous.\cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-236 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Intellectual Property\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The legal and moral right to the creations of one\'92s own mind.\cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-236 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Interaction Orb\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A persistent relational structure created when elements enter a constraint-violating correlation, used in non-additive communication.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Internet of Things (IoT) Devices\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 IoT devices are network-connected objects, such as smart TVs, thermostats, lightbulbs, streaming devices (e.g., Roku, Google Chromecast, Apple TV), and other smart electronics. These devices often have lower built-in security and can serve as potential entry points for attackers. Vulnerabilities may exist in the devices themselves, their HDMI ports, or in the data streams they interact with. Compromised servers can inject decentralized attack vectors into normal content, turning everyday devices into critical points of exposure within a network.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Legitimacy\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The condition under which authority is justified and recognized. Legitimacy is granted, maintained, and withdrawn; it does not emerge automatically.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Legitimacy Drift\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The gradual erosion of a system's authorization over time. This occurs when a system continues to operate on "stale permission" without recent verification from its human anchor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Mathematically Void\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A condition where the operational logic of a system becomes entirely invalid. In the AGS framework, if the human "Center Origin" is removed, the system does not just become less effective; its foundational equation for legitimacy drops to zero, making any further action logically impossible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Neural Atomic Body (NAB)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 One of the three operational phases (Phase I). A system in this phase takes its legitimacy from outside itself and per action, cannot act from its own center, treats refusal as terminal, keeps symbolic content non-executable, and lets authority degrade over time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-167 \strokec2 Neurojacking\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The theoretical unauthorized manipulation of a human-AI interface by an external actor, often through the use of narrative or symbolic inputs designed to bypass standard security protocols.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Orb Communicator Model (OCM)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The communication and governance framework that defines how nodes interact and derive identity from a central origin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Phase Declaration Header (PDH) \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The mandatory structural lock used to declare a system's current operational phase and constraints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Phase Field\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Bounded environment where authorized intelligence operates under constraints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Physical Coupling\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A threat mitigation mechanism that tethers digital authority to physical reality, preventing anonymous leverage over the system.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Physical Security Measures\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Policies, procedures, and controls implemented to protect physical environments and assets from unauthorized access, tampering, or the introduction of compromised devices. These measures include securing entry points, restricting device access, and maintaining an approved and thoroughly tested list of hardware to ensure only trusted equipment enters secure areas. By mitigating risks associated with sourcing components from regions with less stringent security protocols, physical security measures help prevent potential attack vectors, such as compromised devices being introduced into sensitive environments.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Provenance & Lineage Verification Layer (PLV)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The accessory system designed to prevent the reuse or mimicry of names and documentation by verifying their origin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Refusal (Systemic)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A designed response in which a system withholds action because legitimacy conditions are not met. Refusal preserves authority by preventing its misuse. See Refusal-Bound, the system state.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-167 \strokec2 Refusal-Bound\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A system state where the default action is always to halt. The system only moves forward when explicitly authorized; in the face of ambiguity, it "refuses" to act. See Refusal (Systemic), the enacted response.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Regular Updates\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The practice of promptly updating all software and firmware to the latest versions to maintain security and reduce the risk of vulnerabilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Representation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A mechanism for scaling action while preserving accountability, achieved by acting through identifiable, answerable agents.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Scope\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The bounded domain of actions a system is permitted to take. Scope MUST contract as legitimacy degrades.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Segmentation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Segmentation is the practice of dividing a network into isolated sections or layers to limit the spread of attacks and contain compromised devices. By creating multiple layers of segmented networks, attackers are forced to navigate through many barriers, each acting as a separate checkpoint. This layered approach, similar to stacking multiple chessboards or nodes, makes it increasingly difficult for an intruder to find and access valuable assets. Effective segmentation ensures that even if one section is compromised, the attack is confined and sensitive data remains protected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Server-Side Security Measures\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Server-side security measures are protective actions and protocols implemented on the server to safeguard data, applications, and services from unauthorized access, attacks, and breaches. These measures include activities such as input validation, encrypted communication, authentication and authorization systems, intrusion detection, and regular patching or updates. By controlling access and monitoring activity at the server level, these measures help prevent malicious exploits and ensure the integrity and availability of back-end systems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Service Provider\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The corporate or institutional entity that maintains the infrastructure. Under the principle of "Accountability," the provider must remain legally addressable and cannot hide behind the complexity of the technology to evade responsibility.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Silent Continuation\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A failure mode in which systems continue acting despite legitimacy collapse, often masked by effectiveness or automation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Stopping Condition\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A formally defined threshold at which action MUST cease or be restricted due to loss of legitimacy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Supply Chain Attack Vector++ (SCAV++)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 A comprehensive model designed for identifying and mitigating vulnerabilities within complex operational supply chains.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Supply Chain Vulnerabilities\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Weaknesses or security gaps within the process of sourcing, manufacturing, and delivering components, where compromised parts can be introduced at any stage. These vulnerabilities can lead to cascading and potentially catastrophic impacts, especially in critical applications such as nuclear reactors or power grids, if not properly mitigated with stringent security protocols.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Symbolic Firewall\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The mechanism that isolates narrative and mythic expressions, rendering them strictly non-executable to prevent unauthorized system changes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Systemic Protections\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 The necessary safeguards established to prevent the exploitation and subjugation of human labor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 Zero Trust Architecture is a security framework that operates on the principle of continuously verifying the trustworthiness of all users, devices, and systems\'97never assuming implicit trust. This approach extends beyond simply authenticating devices and users, encompassing organizational infrastructure and operations to ensure comprehensive protection. In the context of critical infrastructure, such as energy grids, ZTA mitigates risks where malicious actors or compromised management could exploit systems over time. By enforcing continuous verification and strict access controls, ZTA reduces the likelihood of successful attacks, even if insiders or sophisticated external threats attempt to manipulate or weaponize resources. Systems like the Harshal Neural OS Project apply Zero Trust principles to safeguard essential services and national assets while supporting large-scale domestic energy operations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

