\cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 The Problem (Why This Matters)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Modern institutions regularly claim to be neutral, advisory, informational, or non-governing while simultaneously:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	Issuing rules people MUST follow,\
\'95	Enforcing decisions that affect lives,\
\'95	Shaping behavior through opaque systems,\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Accumulating power over time without ever admitting it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 This creates three widespread failures:\
\pard\tx20\tx290\tx720\pardeftab720\li290\fi-290\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\ls36\ilvl0\cf2 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1.	}\cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Hidden Power \'97 People are affected by authority they are told does not exist.\cb1 \
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 2.	Broken Trust \'97 Disputes arise not because of disagreement, but because power was misrepresented.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 3. Endless Arguments \'97 Debates focus on intent and morality instead of observable behavior. Most conflicts today are not about whether power should exist. They are about power pretending not to exist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\qc\partightenfactor0

\f9 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \uc0\u11835 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 \strokec2 The Core Insight\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Power is not dangerous because it exists. Power becomes dangerous when it is unclear, undeclared, or denied. People can live with authority. People can live with advice. People cannot live with confusion about which one they are facing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 The Proposed Solution (In Plain Language)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 This framework introduces a simple rule: Any system MUST clearly state what kind of power it has, and that statement MUST match its behavior.\
It does this by:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	Defining three clear modes a system can operate in,\
\'95	Requiring systems to declare their mode up front,\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Changing the label automatically if behavior contradicts the claim.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 No one is punished.\
No one is shut down.\
Nothing is outlawed.\
The system only removes the ability to mislabel power.\
The Three Modes (Simply Explained)\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	Refusal-Bound (NAB): \'93We can stop things, but we cannot command you.\'94\
\'95	Witness-Only (CWO): \'93We remember and show what happened, but we NEVER decide.\'94\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Sovereign-Acting (GSRB): \'93We make binding decisions and take responsibility for them.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 None of these are good or bad by default. What matters is honesty about which one is in use.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 What Changes for Ordinary People\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	You can immediately see whether something is advice or a rule.\
\'95	You can tell whether a system is remembering information or deciding outcomes.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	You no longer have to guess where authority is coming from.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 Disagreements become clearer because the type of power is no longer disputed.\
What This Does Not Do\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	It does not remove authority.\
\'95	It does not decide who is right.\
\'95	It does not enforce compliance.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	It does not require belief or trust.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa360\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 It only requires clarity. One-Sentence Summary: This framework matters because it makes power honest about decisions instead of arguing about whether power was secretly used. End of Ground 0 \'b7 v1.3 document.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-112 Orb Communicator Model (OCM)\
