\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 Abstract\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 The Orb Communicator Model (OCM) defines a radiative, center-origin communication and governance system in which all participants derive identity, scope, and ownership from a single immutable origin point. \
Unlike hierarchical or purely peer-to-peer systems, OCM separates communication freedom from ownership provenance, allowing lateral interaction while preserving a provable root of authority. This document formalizes the model, its addressing scheme, ownership semantics, and operational status and guarantees.\
1.Motivation\
Traditional organizational, network, and governance systems su
\f10 \uc0\u64256 
\f1 er from:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	Fragmented authority roots\
\'95	Ambiguous ownership claims\
\'95	Power drift through delegated hierarchy\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Forking identities without detectable lineage breaks\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 OCM is designed to:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	Maintain a single, verifiable origin of ownership\
\'95	Allow unrestricted communication between participants\
\'95	Scale to global stakeholder systems without authority collapse\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	Express influence, responsibility, and scope spatially rather than hierarchically\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

