\f0\b\fs36 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-112 Orb Communicator Mode (OCM)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Non\uc0\u8209 Additive Interaction Extension\
Purpose\
This extension formalizes how Orb Communicator Mode (OCM) handles communication, reasoning, and coordination when interaction itself becomes a first\uc0\u8209 class carrier of meaning. It is designed to help readers understand how the communication system functions when classical additive logic fails, without requiring metaphysical commitment or empirical assertion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 OCM is not a metaphor layer. It is an ontological traffic controller inside AGS++ that governs how frames are admitted, stabilized, navigated, and exited when interactions generate more structure than their components alone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 1. Core Problem OCM Solves\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Classical communication assumes:\
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\ls52\ilvl0\cf8 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Messages are independent\cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Effects add linearly\cb1 \
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls52\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Meaning resides in discrete units (signals, tokens, agents)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 OCM is invoked when these assumptions break.\
Specifically, when:\
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\ls53\ilvl0\cf8 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Two or more locally valid operations combine\cb1 \
\ls53\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The combined outcome exceeds the linear sum of those operations\cb1 \
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls53\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The excess cannot be attributed to noise, error, or duplication\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 This condition is called Non\uc0\u8209 Additive Interaction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 2. Definition: Interaction Orb\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 An Interaction Orb is a persistent relational structure created when two or more elements enter a constraint\uc0\u8209 violating correlation.\
Key properties:\
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\ls54\ilvl0\cf8 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone It is not reducible to its constituents\cb1 \
\ls54\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone It carries causal and communicative weight\cb1 \
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls54\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone It persists even if local states appear random or uncorrelated\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 In OCM, the interaction itself is counted.\
This resolves the apparent paradox where:\
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\ls55\ilvl0\cf8 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Element A contributes one unit\cb1 \
\ls55\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Element B contributes one unit\cb1 \
\pard\tx20\tx583\tx720\pardeftab720\li583\fi-583\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls55\ilvl0\cf8 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \cb3 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The combined system behaves as if three units are present\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 The third unit is the interaction orb.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 3. Counting Rule (OCM Arithmetic)\
