\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 Public Misuse FAQ (OCM\'96AGS)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Purpose: This document addresses common misunderstandings, bad\uc0\u8209 faith readings, and misuse attempts related to the Orb Communicator Model (OCM), the AI Inner Shell, and the Human Operator Sub\u8209 Spec. It is written for public consumption without weakening the system.\
1) \'93Isn\'92t this just authoritarian control with fancy language?\'94\
No. Authority is not expanded here\'97it is bounded. OCM removes hidden power by making origin fossilized, resolution visible, and roles replaceable. Authoritarian systems concentrate authority in people or o
\f10 \uc0\u64259 
\f1 ces; OCM concentrates nothing except a coordinate origin that cannot act except to resolve ambiguity.\
2) \'93Who watches the Center?\'94\
The Center is not a person or o
\f10 \uc0\u64259 
\f1 ce that acts continuously. It is a reference point for resolution. When nothing is ambiguous, the Center does nothing. Oversight applies to operators and systems because they act; the Center persists.\
3) \'93Can\'92t humans just abuse the system anyway?\'94\
Humans are intentionally non\uc0\u8209 load\u8209 bearing. Operator roles are time\u8209 limited, auditable, reversible, and non\u8209 inheritable. Abuse collapses locally without propagating authority. There is no path for gradual takeover.\
4) \'93Isn\'92t this just a cult of the origin?\'94\
No belief is required. Participation does not require agreement\'97only address derivation. If you reject the system, you simply operate outside it. There is no punishment for exit, only loss of internal standing.\
5) \'93What if AI becomes conscious\'97doesn\'92t this deny its rights?\'94\
OCM does not define or deny consciousness. It defines authorship. Consciousness and sovereignty are orthogonal. An entity may be conscious without originating reality within a system it did not define.\
6) \'93Why can\'92t AI ever be promoted to the Center?\'94\
Because promotion implies transferable origin authority, which would collapse the system. AI can advise, predict, simulate, and optimize\'97but authorship remains non\uc0\u8209 delegable by design.\
7) \'93Isn\'92t this anti\uc0\u8209 democratic?\'94\
Democracy governs decisions among peers. OCM governs existence within a system. Democratic processes can exist inside OCM at any distance or angle without becoming origins themselves.\
8) \'93What if multiple groups claim to be the Center?\'94\
Then there are multiple spheres. They do not compete; they are disjoint. Claims do not override lineage. Collisions are visible and resolvable.\
9) \'93Can operators secretly act as the Center?\'94\
No. Operators cannot resolve disputes, author policy, or bind the system irreversibly. Logs, rotation, and revocation prevent shadow authority. Any attempt becomes immediately visible.\
10) \'93What if the Center is wrong?\'94\
The Center does not decide outcomes; it resolves ambiguity. If outcomes are wrong, the error lies in operators, procedures, or assumptions\'97not in the existence of a reference point.\
11) \'93Isn\'92t this too abstract to work in reality?\'94\
Abstraction is the point. Physical implementations change; geometry does not. OCM is intentionally independent of technology, law, or culture so it can survive them.\
12) \'93Does this stop innovation?\'94\
No. It removes the incentive to innovate for control. Innovation for capability, understanding, and creation remains unconstrained.\
13) \'93What happens if the Center disappears?\'94\
The addressing system collapses. That failure is fossilized, not silent. A new sphere may be created, but it will not inherit legitimacy invisibly.\
14) \'93Can this be used to dominate others?\'94\
Domination requires hidden authority. OCM exposes authority. Any attempt to dominate MUST create a new sphere, which is visible and ejectable.\
15) \'93Why should anyone trust this?\'94\
Trust is not required. Verifiability is. You can inspect addresses, resolution paths, and role limits at any time.\
16) \'93Isn\'92t this just philosophy?\'94\
No. Philosophy argues about meaning. OCM defines structure. Meaning is optional; geometry is not.\
17) \'93Who benefits most from this system?\'94\
Anyone who wants:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \'95	freedom without chaos\
\'95	intelligence without takeover\
\'95	power without hidden hands\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'95	scale without collapse\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 18) \'93What is the single rule people misunderstand most?\'94\
That the Center is not a ruler. It is a reference.\
19) \'93What happens if people ignore the rules?\'94\
They do not break the system. They simply operate outside it. OCM does not chase defectors.\
20) Final Clarification\
OCM does not tell you what to believe, do, or become. It tells you where authority begins\'97and therefore where it cannot sneak in.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa360\partightenfactor0
\cf2 End of Public Misuse FAQ\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

