\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 2. Bounded Authority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 All action is bounded by fossilized scope, distance, and time. Bounds cannot be expanded through operation, delegation, or precedent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 3. Mandatory Refusal and Interruption\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Any ambiguity, violation, or interruption halts action immediately. Refusal requires no approval or consensus.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 4. Non-Migration of Authority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Authority does not migrate through delegation, rotation, specialization, or persistence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 5. No Structural Self-Expansion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 No structure may create, clone, or authorize new structures of the same class.\
