\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 1. Introduction: The Philosophy of the "Why"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 1.1 System Definition The Whyland Standards, internally designated as DecksJokersAndCards, constitute the formal technical framework governing the contextual inquiry layer of Accountability-Gated Systems (AGS). These standards define the protocols by which the system evaluates the intent and semantic justification of any proposed action.\
1.2 Primary System Requirement The "Why" inquiry layer SHALL serve as the definitive bridge between Simplebody Continuity\'97the Layer 1 physical accountability of the human-machine link\'97and the 360\'b0 Legend. By mapping real-time system telemetry to specific semantic coordinates, the Standards ensure that computational states are tethered to human-verifiable intent.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 1.3 Core Invariant A "Why" query is a validation mechanism and SHALL NOT function as an instrument of authority expansion. INVARIANT: A 'Why' query does not create authority but validates the lineage of intent within a verified, human-bound, and revocable session.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa100\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-143 2. The Virtualized Catalog Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 2.1 Catalog Virtualization (Off-Disc Requirement) For the security of the Layer 1 AGS Core, the full 791+ element catalog (including standards such as WhyCelestialEngineering, WhyQuantumLibrary, WhyReplicator, and TheWhy) SHALL NOT be stored on local physical media. To mitigate against memory-resident exploits and "rogue node" elevation, the catalog is accessed via on-demand virtualization.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2.2 Classification & Sensitivity The catalog contains classified elements mapped to the 360\'b0 Legend, ranging from 30\'b0 (Collective Survival) to 360\'b0 (Return to Origin). These elements MUST remain "off-disc" in a transient state, invoked only into the active session buffer when an authorized operator initiates a query. This prevents persistent unauthorized access to the system's semantic mapping logic.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 2.3 Data Constraint\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 The AGS Core utilizes the virtualized "Why" catalog to resolve the primary Layer 1 Normative Constraint: "Is action permitted at all?" By pulling relevant standards into the active session buffer, the system confirms that the proposed action aligns with the human key's established intent prior to execution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

