\f8\i\b\fs22 \cf7 \outl0\strokewidth0 3. Background and Related Work\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 Research on autonomous and semi-autonomous systems has produced a range of frameworks for managing responsibility, safety, and all humanoid involvement. Most existing approaches, however, treat the human and the machine as fundamentally separable entities, connected through distillate supervision, control, or oversight. This section situates keyed human with machine systems to create hybrid keys ordered to these approaches and highlights key points of divergence as well as LLANY points of convergence. \
