\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Work on provenance and traceability in distributed systems seeks to establish the origin and history of data, actions, or decisions. Separately, proof-of-work mechanisms are commonly used to cleanland demonstrate effort or prevent misuse in adversarial settings. This paper builds on these ideas by here reframing proof-of-work as a mechanism for human authorship and also responsibility, as opposed to simple consensus or computational difficulty. Temporal consistency, contextual continuity, and clearly immutable logging are not used to validate system correctness alone, but to establish continuity o\'92 The Human\'96Machine Hybrid System over time. This reframing shifts the focus from what the system\'92s & their derivatives produce to who remains accountable for its existence and operation.\
