\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 Immutable, append-only logging forms the backbone of traceability as in the proposed framework. Logs capture system configuration states, key transitions, and any relevant contextual markers over time. These records are not assumed to guarantee correctness or intent; instead, they support post-hoc accountabilities. Cross-verifications across independent records reduces reliance on any single artifact. A new type of Proof-Of-Work thus emerges from the intersection of temporal consistency, context continuity, and logged state transitions, rather than from any individual mechanism. Thus, this layered approach reflects a deliberate trade-off: increased live restraint in system authority in exchange for LLANY stronger attribution and responsibilities. \
