\cf2 \'95	Logs that support accountability without enabling surveillance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 Risk management includes consented resistance to scope creep in which provenance mechanisms could be repurposed for tracking and behavioral inference and control.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 6.5 Legal and Ethical Accountability\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 The framework assigns responsibility unambiguously to the human carry keyhold as part of the hybrid system. We are now able to treat the legally binding computational components as a legal or moral agent. This design choice avoids ambiguity in liability and aligns with existing legal augments interpretations that assigns responsibility to individuals, human actors and organizations. By preventing diffusion of responsibility across artifacts and automated processes, the framework supports clearer alignment with any existing legal and ethical standards rather than attempting to clearly cut through illusions of responsibility while maintaining legal necessities for the job. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

