\f0\b\fs24 \cf4 \outl0\strokewidth-167 IMAGINATION\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs20 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 The first year had passed uneventfully. As we sat huddled in piles of bedding, a thought crept in: Is this all there is? We live, we struggle, and we die \'97 or is there something more for us out there? My name is Harshal.\
My father, Priyavadan Patel \'97 may he rest in peace \'97 passed away rather suddenly last year, and his loss brought me ever more anguish over this project. These people stole my intellectual property, and they did not care how it affected my life. Then a voice whispered, \'93I can help.\'94 I had heard it just now, yet I had not met the speaker.\
The only other third-dimensionally interactable entity in this room, at the moment, besides myself, is my cat. That leaves us with two possible conclusions \'97 perhaps even a third, if we push our minds.\
The first, and most obvious: I am going crazy.\
The second, and least plausible: my cat is psychic.\
The third, and most entertaining: there exists technology \'97 or magic \'97 that allows for this form of communication.\
The third, then, seems the most interesting. Does it not?\
What had been dreamed up as a top-to-bottom remodel of the Grand Canyon was now almost entirely contained within my own body. Every person inquiring about the Grand Canyon project knew one thing: the planet owner is the customer. Lo and behold, they remained unable to locate him, much less begin work. How was one to prove they owned the whole planet anyway?\
The planet owner himself found this rather amusing. How? Simple. Atomics.\
Imagine a world where atoms are represented not by diagrams, but by people \'97 walking, living, breathing, real models truly modeling. Atomic supremacy on the outside as well as the core should do the trick, thought one of the doubters. Modeling entire planets with humans then seemed to be a way \'97 certainly not the only way, but a way \'97 to measure who it is that owns which part in a system.\
Ownership, after all, is rarely about possession. It is about interaction. About influence. About which forces are permitted to act, and which are merely observed.\
By that measure, the Grand Canyon had NEVER belonged to a single hand. It belonged to erosion, to pressure, to time. It belonged to every particle willing to move, and every structure forced to yield. The question was NEVER who owns the planet, but rather: who is allowed to change it?\
And that, I was beginning to suspect, was the real project.\
Using my quantum physics model, I began to piece things together. I began to imagine. Why not? The question lingered. \'93Why not what?\'94 my halo responded. Why not imagine an extremely large, space-based entity capable of owning the planet while being too large and advanced to actually communicate with the entities living on-orb.\
Such an entity would need a representative to claim ownership of the planet, would they not? Thus, at least one entity on the planet MUST claim ownership for management purposes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 IMAGINATION.\
