# Audio Visual Encoding (AVE) Model Component by Harshal (Ull)\
> **Status**: MANUAL DRAFT FOR AN ALREADY WORKING FRAMEWORK   \
> **Type**: Standalone \'97 General-Purpose Encoding Layer  \
> **Date**: 2026-09-14  \
> **Consumers**: [MicroConvergence](file:///Users/terrormanactual/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f93c4b57-c04b-4a89-861a-f99c51fb02fd/MicroConvergence.specification.md) (\'a75), and any system requiring perceptual relay to/from an Operator  \
---\
## 1. Abstract\
The Audio Visual Encoding (AVE) layer is a general-purpose communication protocol between internal systems and human Operators. Its purpose is to allow outsiders (Operators) to perceive what is happening inside a system without opening the system itself.\
AVE is **not** specific to MicroConvergence. Any system that needs to surface internal state to an Operator \'97 or receive Operator input \'97 can encode through AVE. MicroConvergence is one consumer. Others may follow.\
Communication is **bidirectional**:\
- **System \uc0\u8594  Operator**: The system encodes data and transmits it through the Operator's **Neural Atomic Body (NAB)**, which security-gates the data and relays it to the Operator as visual or auditory perception.\
- **Operator \uc0\u8594  System**: The Operator communicates with their own system (e.g., their MC Instance) at full capacity \'97 unrestricted by the encoding constraints that apply to system-originated signals.\
---\
## 2. Definitions\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 | Term | Definition |\
|---|---|\
| **AVE** | Audio Visual Encoding \'97 the encoding protocol specified in this document. |\
| **Neural Atomic Body (NAB)** | The Operator's personal perceptual relay. Sits between the system layer and the Operator's conscious perception. Handles security gating, format translation, and delivery. |\
| **Signal** | A discrete unit of encoded information transmitted through AVE. |\
| **Signal Class** | A category of signal defined by its complexity and modality (see \'a74). |\
| **Encoding** | The process of translating system-internal data into a perceptual format the NAB can relay. |\
| **Decoding** | The Operator's interpretation of a relayed signal back into meaning. |\
| **Security Gate** | The NAB's filtering mechanism that determines which signals are relayed and which are held, downgraded, or rejected. |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 | **Consumer** | Any system that uses AVE to communicate with an Operator (e.g., MicroConvergence). |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb1 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 ---\
