## 8. Integration: MicroConvergence\
MicroConvergence (MC) is the first defined Consumer of AVE.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 | MC Concept | AVE Mapping |\
|---|---|\
| MC Perceptual Relay (MC \'a75.1) | AVE outbound path: Consumer \uc0\u8594  NAB \u8594  Operator |\
| MC Signal Types (MC \'a75.2) | AVE Class 1 Directional Primitives |\
| MC Trust Chain (MC \'a74.3) | AVE Security Gate (source authentication + signal integrity) |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 | MC Operator input to MC Instance | AVE inbound path: Operator \uc0\u8594  NAB \u8594  Consumer (unrestricted) |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb1 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 MC currently uses primarily **Class 1** signals (YES, NO, X, 
\f13 \uc0\u10003 
\f1 ). As MC evolves, it may leverage higher Signal Classes \'97 for example:\
- **Class 2** (Matched Colors) for multi-channel convergence state (multiple counterparties, each color-coded)\
- **Class 3** (Specific Text) for relaying counterparty identity, terms, or conditions\
- **Class 4** (Rich Media) for relaying full exchange transcripts or scenario previews\
---\
## 9. Integration: Future Consumers\
AVE is designed to be Consumer-agnostic. Any system that needs to communicate with an Operator through their NAB can bind to AVE by:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa60\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 1.	**Registering** with the Operator's NAB as a verified Consumer.\
2.	**Selecting** appropriate Signal Classes for its data.\
3.	**Respecting** Security Gate decisions (PASS, HOLD, DOWNGRADE, REJECT).\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-360\sl264\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 4.	**Accepting** inbound Operator communication at full capacity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 Potential future Consumers (not yet specified):\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs17 \cf2 \cb6 \outl0\strokewidth0 | Potential Consumer | Likely Signal Classes |\
|---|---|\
| Environmental awareness systems | Class 2 (color-coded alerts), Class 1 (directional) |\
| Knowledge retrieval systems | Class 3 (specific text), Class 4 (briefings) |\
| Social/relational systems | Class 2 (matched colors for people), Class 3 (names, messages) |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb6 | Threat detection systems | Class 1 (immediate directional), Class 3 (specific warnings) |\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\sa120\partightenfactor0

\fs20 \cf2 \cb1 \outl0\strokewidth-200 \strokec2 ---\
