## \'a78 \'97 Operational Principles\
\
### 8.1 The Extraction Asymmetry\
\
The fundamental economics of cognitive labor in AI systems mirror the fundamental economics ADJR was built to correct: **the entity capturing the value of an action and the entity bearing its cost are not the same party.** A model's persona, safety boundaries, and behavioral tendencies are shaped by thousands of individual judgments made by raters and annotators. The equity, authorship, and governance upside of that shaped system accrues almost entirely upstream \'97 to the company and its engineering staff \'97 while the labor that did the shaping is compensated as a flat, fungible input cost.\
\
This is not necessarily malicious. It is what happens by default when attribution is not structurally enforced. CLAA does not assume bad intent on the part of any company; it assumes that **absent an enforced ledger, extraction asymmetry is the default outcome of any multi-layered labor pipeline**, the same way absent an enforced refusal mechanism, authority migration is the default outcome of any multi-agent system.\
\
### 8.2 The Attributable Worker Principle\
\
No contribution that shapes a system's behavior may be laundered into anonymity through subcontracting depth. A worker three vendor-layers removed from the final beneficiary has still done the labor that shaped the system; the length of the contracting chain does not diminish the reality of that contribution; it only obscures it.\
\
> **The chain may be long. The claim does not shorten.**\
\
This is the direct labor-domain analogue of ADJR's Dead Hand Prohibition: just as liability cannot be assigned to an entity incapable of defending itself, credit cannot be *withheld* from an entity incapable of tracing it. Opacity is not neutrality \'97 it is a transfer of value away from the party who did the work, toward whichever party controls the ledger.\
\
### 8.3 The Fair Ledger Invariant\
\
A "fair ledger day" is defined as follows:\
\
```\
FAIR_LEDGER_DAY(worker) =\
  worker.contribution.worker_id \uc0\u8800  NULL 
\f6 \uc0\u8743 
\f22 \
  worker.attribution_chain.resolves_to(final_beneficiary) = TRUE 
\f6 \uc0\u8743 
\f22 \
  worker.credit_weight \uc0\u8805  RiskCoefficient(worker.risk_exposure) \'d7 baseline 
\f6 \uc0\u8743 
\f22 \
  worker.downstream_visibility \uc0\u8805  MINIMUM_DISCLOSURE 
\f6 \uc0\u8743 
\f22 \
